      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For heavy industrial loads in high-density racking, you should generally prioritize column stacking over interlocking patterns to ensure maximum vertical stability and reduce the risk of rack instability. When handling different weight classes, place the heaviest pallets at the bottom to lower your overall center of gravity and minimize tipping moments. Always verify that your local load charts and safety regulations in Rotterdam are strictly followed before commencing any stacking operations.",
