    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. we're mostly doing column stacking right now but i'm worried about the top layers being a bit uneven. if the pallets aren't perfectly flush, it feels like one slight nudge from a forklift or even just some vibration from the warehouse floor could make the whole stack tip or shift. how can we mitigate that risk of the stacks being disrupted by small, unexpected shifts?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To mitigate risks from uneven pallets, ensure you are using appropriate shrink wrap or wood wedge bars to secure both the load and the stack before forklift interaction. When placing full loads onto empty racks, try to align them with existing full bays and vertical boundaries whenever possible to create a more stable structure. Finally, conduct regular stability checks and consider specialized load bars across the entire stack if your loads are extremely heavy or mobile.",
      "source": "target",
