      "content": "To account for unpredictable disturbances, you should implement rigorous seismic and vibration testing to quantify how much lateral movement your stacks can withstand before becoming unstable. Installing additional cladding or netting over the perimeter of your high-density racks will physically block small movements that could otherwise propagate into a catastrophic collapse. Ultimately, the most effective control measure is rigorous worker training on strict forklift operating procedures and frequent visual inspections to catch any subtle shifts before they grow.",
